<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs mostly weaker, Dow dips in late trade.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs mostly weaker, Dow dips in late trade.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were mostly weaker in late New York trade while the Dow Jones Index was easier but off its session low. By 8 a.m. NZT the Dow was off 13.08 points at 6,793.08.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	  Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$16 3/8	 +0 1/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$31 3/8	 -0 1/2 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$28 3/8	 -0 1/4 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 1/4	 -0 1/4 *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$15 1/8	 +0 1/8 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$78	     -1 7/8 *</p>
<p>Thistle	  N.Y.    192		 -0 1/2</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  35		  -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  255		 +1 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col London  153		   +3/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  154		   +2</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$3.30		-5</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.56		-2</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  A$2.65		-5</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
